#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Introduction {#1-introduction}"
msgstr "1. Introduzione {#1-introduction}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bits, gates, and circuits are the basic building blocks of quantum computing. You will learn quantum computation with the circuit model using quantum bits and gates, and also review the superposition, measurement, and entanglement.\n"
msgstr "Bit, gate e circuiti sono i mattoni fondamentali del calcolo quantistico. Imparerai la computazione quantistica con il modello a circuiti usando bit quantistici e gate, e ripasserai anche la sovrapposizione, la misura e l'entanglement.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this lesson you will learn:\n"
"- Single-qubit gates\n"
"- Bloch sphere\n"
"- Superposition\n"
"- Measurement\n"
"- Two-qubit gates and entanglement state\n"
msgstr ""
"In questa lezione imparerai:\n"
"- gate a qubit singolo\n"
"- Sfera di Bloch\n"
"- Sovrapposizione\n"
"- Misura\n"
"- gate a due qubit e stato di entanglement\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At the end of this lecture, you will learn about circuit depth, which is essential for utility-scale quantum computing.\n"
msgstr "Alla fine di questa lezione imparerai la profondità del circuito, fondamentale per il calcolo quantistico su scala utility.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Computation as a diagram {#2-computation-as-a-diagram}"
msgstr "2. La computazione come diagramma {#2-computation-as-a-diagram}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When using qubits or bits, we need to manipulate them in order to turn the inputs we have into the outputs we need. For the simplest programs with very few bits, it is useful to represent this process in a diagram known as a *circuit diagram*.\n"
msgstr "Quando si usano qubit o bit, è necessario manipolarli per trasformare gli input che abbiamo negli output di cui abbiamo bisogno. Per i programmi più semplici con pochissimi bit, è utile rappresentare questo processo in un diagramma noto come *diagramma di circuito*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The bottom-left figure is an example of a classical circuit, and the bottom-right figure is an example of a quantum circuit. In both cases, the inputs are on the left and the outputs are on the right, while the operations are represented by symbols. The symbols used for the operations are called “gates”, mostly for historical reasons.\n"
msgstr "La figura in basso a sinistra è un esempio di circuito classico, quella in basso a destra è un esempio di circuito quantistico. In entrambi i casi, gli input si trovano a sinistra e gli output a destra, mentre le operazioni sono rappresentate da simboli. I simboli usati per le operazioni sono chiamati \"gate\", principalmente per ragioni storiche.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![\"classical logic and quantum circuit\"](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/classical-vs-quantum.avif)\n"
msgstr "![\"circuito logico classico e circuito quantistico\"](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/classical-vs-quantum.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Single-qubit quantum gate {#3-single-qubit-quantum-gate}"
msgstr "3. gate quantistico a qubit singolo {#3-single-qubit-quantum-gate}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.1 Quantum state and Bloch sphere {#31-quantum-state-and-bloch-sphere}"
msgstr "3.1 Stato quantistico e sfera di Bloch {#31-quantum-state-and-bloch-sphere}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A qubit's state is represented as a superposition of $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$. An arbitrary quantum state is represented as\n"
msgstr "Lo stato di un qubit è rappresentato come una sovrapposizione di $|0\\rangle$ e $|1\\rangle$. Uno stato quantistico arbitrario è rappresentato come\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle =\\alpha|0\\rangle+ \\beta|1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle =\\alpha|0\\rangle+ \\beta|1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are complex numbers such that $|\\alpha|^2+|\\beta|^2=1$.\n"
msgstr "dove $\\alpha$ e $\\beta$ sono numeri complessi tali che $|\\alpha|^2+|\\beta|^2=1$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$ are vectors in the two-dimensional complex vector space:\n"
msgstr "$|0\\rangle$ e $|1\\rangle$ sono vettori nello spazio vettoriale complesso bidimensionale:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|0\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"|1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0\\\\1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|0\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"|1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0\\\\1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Therefore, an arbitrary quantum state is also represented as\n"
msgstr "Pertanto, uno stato quantistico arbitrario è rappresentato anche come\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\alpha\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\ 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} + \\beta\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\ \\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\alpha\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\ 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} + \\beta\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\ \\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "From this, we can see that the state of a quantum bit is a unit vector in a two-dimensional complex inner product space with an orthonormal basis of $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$. It is normalized to 1.\n"
msgstr "Da questo si può vedere che lo stato di un bit quantistico è un vettore unitario in uno spazio con prodotto interno complesso bidimensionale con base ortonormale $|0\\rangle$ e $|1\\rangle$. È normalizzato a 1.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\psi|\\psi\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha^* & \\beta^*\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\\n"
"\\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = 1\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\psi|\\psi\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha^* & \\beta^*\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\\n"
"\\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = 1\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ |\\psi\\rangle =\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\ \\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}$ is also called the statevector.\n"
msgstr ""
"$ |\\psi\\rangle =\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha \\\\ \\beta\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}$ è anche chiamato statevector.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A single-qubit quantum state is also represented as\n"
msgstr "Uno stato quantistico a qubit singolo è rappresentato anche come\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"=\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}|0\\rangle+e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}|1\\rangle\n"
"=\\left( \\begin{pmatrix} \\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\\\ e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"=\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}|0\\rangle+e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}|1\\rangle\n"
"=\\left( \\begin{pmatrix} \\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\\\ e^{i\\varphi}\\sin\\frac{\\theta}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\right)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $\\theta$ and $\\varphi$ are the angles of the Bloch sphere in the following figure.\n"
msgstr "dove $\\theta$ e $\\varphi$ sono gli angoli della sfera di Bloch nella figura seguente.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Bloch sphere](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/bloch.avif)\n"
"In the next few code cells, we will build up basic calculations from constituent pieces in Qiskit. We'll construct an empty circuit and then add quantum operations, discussing the gates and visualizing their effects as we go.\n"
"You can run the cell by \"Shift\" + \"Enter\". Import the libraries first.\n"
msgstr ""
"![Sfera di Bloch](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/bloch.avif)\n"
"Nelle prossime celle di codice costruiremo i calcoli di base a partire dai componenti fondamentali di Qiskit. Creeremo un circuito vuoto e aggiungeremo operazioni quantistiche, discutendo i gate e visualizzando i loro effetti man mano che procediamo.\n"
"Puoi eseguire la cella con \"Shift\" + \"Invio\". Importa prima le librerie.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare the quantum circuit {#prepare-the-quantum-circuit}"
msgstr "Preparare il circuito quantistico {#prepare-the-quantum-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will create and draw a single-qubit circuit.\n"
msgstr "Creeremo e disegneremo un circuito a qubit singolo.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/fdef9137-9e39-4b05-afa9-9091766053f6-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output della cella di codice precedente](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/fdef9137-9e39-4b05-afa9-9091766053f6-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "X gate {#x-gate}"
msgstr "gate X {#x-gate}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The X gate is a $\\pi$ rotation around the $x$ axis of the Bloch sphere.\n"
"Applying the X gate to $|0\\rangle$ results in $|1\\rangle$, and applying the X gate to $|1\\rangle$ results in $|0\\rangle$, so it is an operation similar to the classical NOT gate, and is also known as bit flip. The matrix representation of the X gate is below.\n"
msgstr ""
"Il gate X è una rotazione di $\\pi$ attorno all'asse $x$ della sfera di Bloch.\n"
"Applicare il gate X a $|0\\rangle$ dà come risultato $|1\\rangle$, e applicare il gate X a $|1\\rangle$ dà come risultato $|0\\rangle$, quindi è un'operazione simile al gate NOT classico, ed è anche noto come bit flip. La rappresentazione matriciale del gate X è la seguente.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"X = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"X = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/b3468430-0cbc-44ab-bd21-901436662a4b-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output della cella di codice precedente](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/b3468430-0cbc-44ab-bd21-901436662a4b-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In IBM Quantum&reg;, the initial state is set to $|0\\rangle$, so the quantum circuit above in matrix representation is\n"
msgstr "In IBM Quantum&reg;, lo stato iniziale è impostato a $|0\\rangle$, quindi il circuito quantistico sopra in rappresentazione matriciale è\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"X|0\\rangle=  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\ 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\ 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = |1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"X|0\\rangle=  \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\ 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\ 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} = |1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, let's run this circuit using a statevector simulator.\n"
msgstr "Ora eseguiamo questo circuito usando un simulatore di statevector.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/efb727e8-f51e-4903-aa0f-e4c099316815-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output della cella di codice precedente](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/efb727e8-f51e-4903-aa0f-e4c099316815-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Vertical vector is displayed as row vector, with complex numbers (the imaginary part is indexed by $j$ ).\n"
msgstr "Il vettore verticale è visualizzato come vettore riga, con numeri complessi (la parte immaginaria è indicizzata da $j$).\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "H gate {#h-gate}"
msgstr "gate H {#h-gate}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Hadamard gate is a $\\pi$ rotation around an axis halfway between the $x$ and $z$ axes on the Bloch sphere. Applying the H gate to $|0\\rangle$ creates a superposition state such as $\\frac{|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}$. The matrix representation of the H gate is below.\n"
msgstr "Il gate di Hadamard è una rotazione di $\\pi$ attorno a un asse a metà strada tra gli assi $x$ e $z$ della sfera di Bloch. Applicare il gate H a $|0\\rangle$ crea uno stato di sovrapposizione come $\\frac{|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}$. La rappresentazione matriciale del gate H è la seguente.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/574c35f0-26a9-423a-8d65-7140ba7398e3-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output della cella di codice precedente](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/574c35f0-26a9-423a-8d65-7140ba7398e3-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/7adf0e93-6db3-4aa8-800f-c91c8cc46001-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output della cella di codice precedente](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/7adf0e93-6db3-4aa8-800f-c91c8cc46001-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is\n"
"$$\n"
"H|0\\rangle= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.707 \\\\\n"
"0.707\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Questo è\n"
"$$\n"
"H|0\\rangle= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.707 \\\\\n"
"0.707\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This superposition state is so common and important, that it is given its own symbol:\n"
msgstr "Questo stato di sovrapposizione è così comune e importante da avere un suo simbolo:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|+\\rangle \\equiv \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|+\\rangle \\equiv \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle).\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By applying the $H$ gate on the $|0\\rangle$, we created a superposition of $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$ where measurement in the computational basis (along z in the Bloch sphere picture) would give you each state with equal probabilities.\n"
msgstr "Applicando il gate $H$ a $|0\\rangle$, abbiamo creato una sovrapposizione di $|0\\rangle$ e $|1\\rangle$ in cui una misura nella base computazionale (lungo z nella rappresentazione della sfera di Bloch) darebbe ciascuno stato con uguale probabilità.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "$|-\\rangle$ state {#rangle-state}"
msgstr "Stato $|-\\rangle$ {#rangle-state}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You might have guessed that there is a corresponding  $|-\\rangle$ state:\n"
"$$\n"
"|-\\rangle \\equiv \\frac{|0\\rangle -|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"$$\n"
"To create this state, first apply an X gate to make $|1\\rangle$, then apply an H gate.\n"
msgstr ""
"Potresti aver intuito che esiste uno stato $|-\\rangle$ corrispondente:\n"
"$$\n"
"|-\\rangle \\equiv \\frac{|0\\rangle -|1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"$$\n"
"Per creare questo stato, applica prima un gate X per ottenere $|1\\rangle$, poi applica un gate H.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/b8e96fc4-6708-415e-b8fc-ac69eaeae750-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output della cella di codice precedente](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/b8e96fc4-6708-415e-b8fc-ac69eaeae750-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/f42b82aa-7a15-4f81-8530-b997d4c6e0de-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output della cella di codice precedente](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/bits-gates-and-circuits/extracted-outputs/f42b82aa-7a15-4f81-8530-b997d4c6e0de-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is\n"
msgstr "Questo è\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H|1\\rangle= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\\\n"
"1 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\\\n"
"-1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.707 \\\\\\\n"
"-0.707\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle) = |-\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H|1\\rangle= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\\\n"
"1 & -1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
" =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\\\n"
"-1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0.707 \\\\\\\n"
"-0.707\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle) = |-\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying the $H$ gate on $|1\\rangle$ results in an equal superposition of $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$, but the sign of $|1\\rangle$ is negative.\n"
msgstr "Applicando il gate $H$ a $|1\\rangle$ si ottiene una sovrapposizione uguale di $|0\\rangle$ e $|1\\rangle$, ma il segno di $|1\\rangle$ è negativo.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "3.2 Single-qubit quantum state and unitary evolution {#32-single-qubit-quantum-state-and-unitary-evolution}"
msgstr "3.2 Stato quantistico a qubit singolo ed evoluzione unitaria {#32-single-qubit-quantum-state-and-unitary-evolution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The actions of all the gates we have seen so far have been *unitary*, which means they can be represented by a unitary operator. In other words, the output state can be obtained by acting on the initial state with a unitary matrix:\n"
msgstr "Le azioni di tutti i gate che abbiamo visto finora sono state *unitarie*, il che significa che possono essere rappresentate da un operatore unitario. In altre parole, lo stato di output si ottiene applicando allo stato iniziale una matrice unitaria:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi^{'}\\rangle = U|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi^{'}\\rangle = U|\\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A unitary matrix is a matrix satisfying\n"
msgstr "Una matrice unitaria è una matrice che soddisfa\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger}U =U U^{\\dagger} = I.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger}U =U U^{\\dagger} = I.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In terms of quantum computer operation, we would say that applying a quantum gate to the qubit evolves the quantum state. Common single-qubit gates include the following.\n"
msgstr "In termini di operazione del computer quantistico, diremmo che applicare un gate quantistico al qubit fa evolvere lo stato quantistico. I gate a qubit singolo più comuni includono i seguenti.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli gates:\n"
msgstr "gate di Pauli:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"X = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= |0\\rangle \\langle 1|+|1\\rangle \\langle 0|\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"X = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= |0\\rangle \\langle 1|+|1\\rangle \\langle 0|\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Y = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & -i \\\\\n"
"i & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= -i|0\\rangle \\langle 1|+i|1\\rangle \\langle 0|\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Y = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & -i \\\\\n"
"i & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= -i|0\\rangle \\langle 1|+i|1\\rangle \\langle 0|\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Z = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= |0\\rangle \\langle 0|-|1\\rangle \\langle 1|\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Z = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & -1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= |0\\rangle \\langle 0|-|1\\rangle \\langle 1|\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where the outer product was calculated as follows:\n"
"$$\n"
"|0\\rangle \\langle 0|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"|1\\rangle \\langle 0|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"dove il prodotto esterno è stato calcolato come segue:\n"
"$$\n"
"|0\\rangle \\langle 0|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"|1\\rangle \\langle 0|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|0\\rangle \\langle 1|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"|1\\rangle \\langle 1|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|0\\rangle \\langle 1|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 \\\\\n"
"0\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"|1\\rangle \\langle 1|=\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 \\\\\n"
"1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 1\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"=\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & 1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Other typical single-qubit gates:\n"
"$$\n"
"H= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix},\\quad\n"
"S = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & i \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"T = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & exp(i\\pi/4) \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Altri gate a qubit singolo tipici:\n"
"$$\n"
"H= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 1 \\\\\n"
"1 & -1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix},\\quad\n"
"S = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & i \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\n"
"T = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 \\\\\n"
"0 & exp(i\\pi/4) \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"R_x(\\theta) = e^{-i\\theta X/2} = cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}I - i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2}X = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} &  -i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"-i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} & cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"R_x(\\theta) = e^{-i\\theta X/2} = cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}I - i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2}X = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} &  -i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"-i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} & cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"R_y(\\theta) = e^{-i\\theta Y/2} = cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}I - i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2}Y = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} &  - sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} & cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"R_y(\\theta) = e^{-i\\theta Y/2} = cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}I - i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2}Y = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} &  - sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} & cos\\frac{\\theta}{2} \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"R_z(\\theta) = e^{-i\\theta Z/2} = cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}I - i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2}Z = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"e^{-i\\theta /2} &  0 \\\\\n"
"0 & e^{i\\theta /2} \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"R_z(\\theta) = e^{-i\\theta Z/2} = cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}I - i sin \\frac{\\theta}{2}Z = \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"e^{-i\\theta /2} &  0 \\\\\n"
"0 & e^{i\\theta /2} \\\\\n"
"\\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The meaning and use of these are described in more detail in the [Basics of Quantum Information](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information) course.\n"
msgstr "Il significato e l'uso di questi gate sono descritti in modo più dettagliato nel corso [Fondamenti di Informazione Quantistica](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information).\n"

